      "writtenOn": "2023-09-18T20:09:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of grouping two different callback registrations in one `conflatedCallbackFlow`, we should separate them into two separate flows. (A `conflatedCallbackFlow` is intended to be used for exactly one callback.)\n\nI\u0027m guessing that the reason it\u0027s registered here is because the `imsStateCallback` doesn\u0027t emit any state that can be `collect`ed on, it just registers other callbacks? I wonder if we can use some `flatMapLatest` magic to help us here. `flatMapLatest` lets us switch between different flows based on a value. Here\u0027s some pseudocode of what I\u0027m picturing:\n\n```\n// Translates the `ImsStateCallback` into a `Flow\u003cImsState\u003e`\nval imsRegistrationState: Flow\u003cImsState\u003e \u003d conflatedCallbackFlow {\n       val callback \u003d  object : ImsStateCallback() {\n           override fun onAvailable() { trySend(ImsState.AVAILABLE) }\n           override fun onUnavailable() { trySend(ImsState.UNAVAILABLE) }\n           override fun onError() { trySend(ImsState.ERROR) }\n        }\n        // register \u0026 unregister callback\n    }\n     \n// Translates the `ImsMmTelManager.CapabilityCallback` into a `Flow\u003cImsCapabilities\u003e`        \nval imsCapabilities \u003d conflatedCallbackFlow {\n  val capabilityCallback \u003d\n        object : ImsMmTelManager.CapabilityCallback() {\n            override fun onCapabilitiesStatusChanged(config: MmTelCapabilities) {\n                trySend(ImsCapabilities(voiceCapable \u003d config.isCapable(MmTelCapabilities.CAPABILITY_TYPE_VOICE),\n                videoCapable \u003d config.isCapable(MmTelCapabilities.CAPABILITY_TYPE_VIDEO),\n                )\n            }\n        }\n        // register \u0026 unregister callback\n}    \n\n// What this flow does: When IMS becomes available, use the `imsCapabilites` flow\n// defined above to fetch the `voiceCapable` status. When IMS is unavailable or has\n// an error, stop using the `imsCapabilites` flow, and instead just define\n// `isVoiceCapable` as `false`.\noverride val isVoiceCapable \u003d\n  imsRegistrationState.flatMapLatest { state -\u003e\n    if (state \u003d\u003d State.AVAILABLE) {\n      imsCapabilites.map { it.voiceCapable }\n    } else {\n      flowOf(false)\n    }\n  }\n  \n// Similar for isVideoCapable  \n```\n\nNote that `ImsState` and `ImsCapabilities` would be data classes that are defined internally to SysUI.\n\nLet me know if that works for this use case.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 181,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 197,
        "endChar": 17
      },
